.TH BLUETUITH-RS 1 "2026-11-04" "bluetuith-rs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bluetuith-rs \- a full-featured Bluetooth manager for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bluetuith-rs
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bluetuith-rs
is a terminal user interface for managing Bluetooth adapters and devices.
It talks to BlueZ over the system D-Bus and provides adapter control, device
discovery/pairing/connection, OBEX Object Push file transfers, AVRCP media
playback, PAN networking and audio profile views. The interface is built with
ratatui and supports the mouse, configurable keybindings and multiple colour
themes.
.PP
With
.B \-\-demo
the application runs against a built-in simulated adapter, so it can be used
(and tested) on machines without Bluetooth hardware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list-adapters
List available adapters and exit.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-generate
Write a default configuration file and exit.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-adapter " " \fINAME\fR
Adapter to use (e.g. hci0 or a MAC address).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-receive-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Directory for received OBEX files.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-gsm-apn " " \fIAPN\fR
APN for DUN dial-up networking.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-gsm-number " " \fINUMBER\fR
Number to dial for DUN (default *99#).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-adapter-states " " \fILIST\fR
Startup states, e.g. 'powered:yes,discoverable:yes,scan:no'.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-connect-bdaddr " " \fIMAC\fR
Auto-connect this device on startup.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-no-warning
Suppress the unavailable-features banner.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-no-help-display
Hide the bottom keybinding strip.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-confirm-on-quit
Ask for confirmation before quitting.
.TP
.B "\-\-no-confirm-on-quit"
Quit immediately.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-disable-obex-services
Disable OBEX services.
.TP
.B "\-\-show-hidden-files"
Show hidden files in the file picker.
.TP
.B "\-\-scan-on-start"
Start discovery at launch.
.TP
.BR "\-\-theme " \fINAME\fR
Palette: Midnight, Nord, Catppuccin, Dracula, Gruvbox, Tokyo Night,
Rosé Pine, Solarized or Daylight.
.TP
.BR "\-\-accent " \fI#RRGGBB\fR
Override the accent colour.
.TP
.BR "\-\-default-sort " \fIKEY\fR
Name, Address, Rssi, Battery, State or Kind.
.TP
.BR "\-\-config " \fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate configuration file.
.TP
.B "\-\-demo"
Run against a simulated adapter (no BlueZ required).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
Navigate with the arrow keys. c connect/disconnect, p pair, t trust,
b block, d remove, o power, S discoverable, P pairable, s scan,
a change adapter, f send files, v transfers, m media player,
n network options, A audio profiles, i device info, / search,
F2 details, F3 sort, F4 theme, F6 log, Ctrl+p command palette,
Alt+m menu, ? help, Q quit, Ctrl+z suspend, Ctrl+x cancel, Esc close.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bluetuith-rs/config.toml
User configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Options may also be set through BLUETUITH_RS_* variables (the BLUETUITH_*
forms used by the original bluetuith are accepted as aliases).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR bluetoothd (8)
